# ---------------------------------------------------------------- hard rule
#
# NO Call of Duty data, ever. This repository ships extraction CODE; the
# player supplies the game. Anything below is a shape that game data arrives
# in — if one of these ever shows up in `git status`, something is wrong.
*.pk3
*.iwd
*.iwi
*.d3dbsp
*.xmodel
*.xmodel_export
*.xanim
*.xanim_export
*.gsc
*.ff
*.bik
*.roq
*.fodpak

# Export output. The generator writes a package; it never belongs in here.
/out/
/output/
/dist/
# build_exporter.py's PyInstaller scratch directory. Untracked it
# makes every checkout look dirty, which matters because the
# release scripts warn when a payload is built from uncommitted work.
/Builds/

# CI-built cod_asset_importer extensions, fetched with `make importer-fetch`.
# Build outputs of github.com/anarqz/cod-asset-importer, reproducible from
# that repo's workflow, ~11 MB of binaries per refresh.
/packaging/importers/

# Blender is downloaded to a per-user cache at runtime, never into the tree.
/blender/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
build/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------- misc
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
